{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:e69c63119df1c1f9","name":"Imperial Knight","source":{"id":"source:reference-e69c63119df1c1f9","title":"Imperial Knight","revision":25226,"timestamp":"2024-11-13T20:11:10Z","sha256":"99c04f91a735a41fda922f825da8b0861eeced16383b518549f37e5f87cee473","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=25226","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Imperial%20Knight&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-e69c63119df1c1f9","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Legacy Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Legacy_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["The Imperial Knights"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Imperial_Knights","referenceId":"reference:f83f5f82e44c1559"}," are ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi","referenceId":"reference:0b0e48747027a29d"}," who dedicate themselves to the preservation of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Fel Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Fel_Empire","referenceId":"reference:45bef1c82bffe9c1"}," and the defense of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Emperor Roan Fel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Emperor_Roan_Fel"},"- not unlike the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Royal Guards"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Royal_Guards"}," that once protected ",{"tag":"a","children":["Emperor Palpatine"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Emperor_Palpatine"},", though their training in ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," distinguishes them from that organization. Despite opinions to the contrary, Imperial Knights are every bit as capable in the use of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," as their Jedi counterparts, though their training has considerably more martial focus. During the height of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith-Imperial War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith-Imperial_War"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Imperial Knights"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Imperial_Knights","referenceId":"reference:f83f5f82e44c1559"}," were forbidden from participating in the fighting. Instead, they served as the Emperor's personal guard.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["At any given time, there are as few as a dozen Imperial Knights or as many as three score. Casualties within the Order have been high since ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darth Krayt"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darth_Krayt","referenceId":"reference:c6d0b6bc88280f92"}," declared himself Emperor. The remaining Imperial Knights continue to serve ",{"tag":"a","children":["Roan Fel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Roan_Fel","referenceId":"reference:b68838dc4018d9d2"}," closely, with many fighting an insurgent war against ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"}," and their Imperial forces.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Recruitment within ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Imperial Knights"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Imperial_Knights","referenceId":"reference:f83f5f82e44c1559"}," is limited to individuals who demonstrate both Force potential and loyalty to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Roan Fel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Roan_Fel","referenceId":"reference:b68838dc4018d9d2"},". Like ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"},", Imperial Knights are permitted to take on apprentices, but only one at a time and only once they have mastered their own skills to a sufficient degree. Apprenticeships are personally approved by the Emperor, as are promotions within the structure of the Order. Only the highest ranking Imperial Knight is designated as a \"Master,\" subject to Roan Fel's approval.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Imperial Knights reject the use of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"}," of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},", yet true ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi","referenceId":"reference:0b0e48747027a29d"}," still feel that ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Imperial Knights"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Imperial_Knights","referenceId":"reference:f83f5f82e44c1559"}," lack a balanced approach to their use of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},". Controlling fear and managing one's emotions in the face of adversity is paramount to the ideology of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Imperial Knights"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Imperial_Knights","referenceId":"reference:f83f5f82e44c1559"},", as is loyalty to their Emperor. They are warriors first and foremost, not negotiators, and they make no excuses for this fact.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Examples of Imperial Knights in Star Wars:"]}," Sigel Dare, Antares Draco, Marasiah Fel, Mohrgan Fel, Roan Fel, Ganner Krieg, Azlyn Rae, Treis Sinde, Elke Vetter.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Prerequisites:"]}," To qualify to become an Imperial Knight, a character must fulfill the following criteria:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Base Attack Bonus"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Base_Attack_Bonus"},":"]}," +7"]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Trained Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trained_Skills"},":"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use the Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_the_Force","referenceId":"reference:74883d1dd46b87fe"}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Feats"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Feats","referenceId":"reference:9194ccf56b9cace0"},":"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Armor Proficiency (Light)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Armor_Proficiency_(Light)","referenceId":"reference:5c5fd1ac409e0220"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Armor Proficiency (Medium)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Armor_Proficiency_(Medium)","referenceId":"reference:466f1c0788c7f68d"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Sensitivity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Sensitivity","referenceId":"reference:5202cab02f367bcf"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Proficiency (Lightsabers)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Proficiency_(Lightsabers)"}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Special:"]}," Must be a sworn defender of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Emperor Roan Fel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Emperor_Roan_Fel"},"."]}]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Game Rule Information"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Imperial Knights have the following game statistics: \n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["LEVEL\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["BASE ATTACK BONUS"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/BASE_ATTACK_BONUS"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["CLASS FEATURES\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["\n"],"rowspan":6},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["LEVEL\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["BASE ATTACK BONUS"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/BASE_ATTACK_BONUS"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["CLASS FEATURES\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1st\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children"